egal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"}}],"rulings":[{"oracle_id":"a3c35742-e306-49b6-b042-db4f685c6f86","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc","comment":"This is not a targeted ability, so it deals damage to creatures that can’t be targeted by spells and abilities."},{"oracle_id":"94fa21f1-826a-4d51-9ccd-d72e5cf13f3d","published_at":"2017-02-09","source":"wotc","comment":"When the enchanted artifact is put into a graveyard, Gremlin Infestation's controller creates the Gremlin token."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"Abilities that Slivers grant, as well as power/toughness boosts, are cumulative. However, for some abilities, like indestructible and the ability granted by Belligerent Sliver, having more than one instance of the ability doesn’t provide any additional benefit."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"If you change the creature type of a Sliver you control so it’s no longer a Sliver, it will no longer be affected by its own ability. Its ability will continue to affect other Sliver creatures you control."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"Slivers in this set affect only Sliver creatures you control. They don’t grant bonuses to your opponents’ Slivers. This is the same way Slivers from the Magic 2014 core set worked, while Slivers in earlier sets granted bonuses to all Slivers."},{"oracle_id":"e4fe33e7-b952-4152-8c83-81d948756d2f","published_at":"2014-07-18","source":"wotc","comment":"Damage dealt to a Sliver with indestructible is still marked on that creature. If it has lethal damage marked on it and it loses indestructible (perhaps because Sliver Hivelord leaves the battlefield), it will be destroyed."},{"oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc","comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat."},{"oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc","comment":"When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled."},{"oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc","comment":"If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield."},{"oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc","comment":"Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist."},{"oracle_id":"6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc","comment":"The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it."},{"oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc","comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it."},{"oracle_id":"049d1fb2-cce7-40e7-a633-e84cf9782d89","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc","comment":"If you Donate an Aura, it stays where it is, but the targeted player now controls it."},{"oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc","comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step."},{"oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc","comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\"."}]}
